<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:45Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Norway seizes Russian ship in Svalbard to compensate Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da625dd8462a1e4086d112501e2215445f8ecdc11456312d229f65c26b06b64d</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-seizes-russian-ship-in-svalbard-to-compensate-ukraine/a-78889005--e844c371e0fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-seizes-russian-ship-in-svalbard-to-compensate-ukraine/a-78889005?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Norway have seized a Russian ship, the Professor Molchanov, on a court order sought and obtained by Naftogaz in Ukraine. Russia has protested the move, which stems from its refusal to pay Naftogaz damages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Macron visits Bayeux Tapestry with King Charles, PM Andy Burnham</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bea6e375cd3716b189ecf1ca2712cdb133bf64436933441b014a16219be91cc</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317--6e79a02657ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-visits-bayeux-tapestry-with-king-charles-pm-andy-burnham/a-78772317?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is on a shorter-term visit to the UK than the renowned on-loan 11th century tapestry. He viewed the ancient artwork with the UK monarch and relatively new Prime Minister Andy Burnham.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU summons Russian envoy over failed Leipzig drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a47b8dc832c72c1c8774d47d2aef6d9de435a7c84faf8bdd54382d8d1ab09101</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280--3cbf965ee0be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said the attempted attack had "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism." She said the EU was summoning a Russian envoy, with France announcing a similar step.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russia threatens 'devastating' Baltic response</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37e4a02d3eb1b2a383bbbcdbb043e0c070f2d0c93ed1be3a6e4f3d34773d537f</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T00:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421--4d6b6f67645b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-threatens-devastating-baltic-response/live-78582421?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Any escalation in the Baltic region will lead to a significant response, Moscow said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany says Russia behind attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaad8694f4312b86abf4ea0cc8affc871c8ac6541c79dfdeeed410cb8d00394f</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T22:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589--8f1b490f01fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators believe an explosives-laden drone was deliberately targeting a Ukrainian cargo aircraft at Leipzig/Halle airport in early August. The German government said on Tuesday that it held Russia "responsible."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mladic's death, Bosnia and Serbia's unfinished reckoning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88d90a5db0e0ab923ffd37d6db27654625d2b4b26f35218c5fe7f4914fa6f984</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733--ecbac0d391f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Ratko Mladic did not close a dark chapter of European history; it reopened old wounds. The ideology that created him lives on. The Dayton peace agreement ended the war, not the divisions that produced it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's new King Haakon VIII takes oath in parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa6e3772a4042529c26ed7ba96a226823ae0cbc2b098742a2fed1be1fe7c1635</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923--a61407b67d7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new king swore to uphold the constitution in parliament in Oslo, the first major institutional step of his reign. Haakon VIII's wife Queen Mette-Marit had to skip the event in the aftermath of her lung transplant.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US irks Germany, Europe with Russian G20 invite, press bans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c865e3c8851c6ee890c7002f512009108175a82c5487a8a644a528603324bbb3</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919--633a7d6f1632.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's finance minister is at the G20 meeting in Asheville but some key US press corps members are not. The mood was already tense amid the lengthy Iran war and Trump's renewed beef with neighbor Canada.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Greece, Turkey clash over protected Aegean marine areas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6f0ed91dcc69c5d65bd0be5b1e13ff966b10cf29c1b3f915db5a295da9b3dac</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/greece-turkey-clash-over-protected-aegean-marine-areas/a-78550021--e8c2e88d0a18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/greece-turkey-clash-over-protected-aegean-marine-areas/a-78550021?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey has announced the creation of two protected zones in a disputed area of the Aegean Sea, sparking an angry reaction from Greece. Does this mark a new chapter in a long-running dispute between the two countries?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russian-American heads Trump's planned Caucasus trade route</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c2aeb9f24871f5e8ec2730081d3af7fc4ffece92576d88336f73e3aa8ac1d60</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-american-heads-trump-s-planned-caucasus-trade-route/a-78547064--fc8b44c9dfea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-american-heads-trump-s-planned-caucasus-trade-route/a-78547064?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Russian-born businessman heads the investment fund financing the so-called "Trump Route," a planned corridor through Armenia linking Azerbaijan with Nakhchivan. Who is Konstantin Sokolov, and what role does he play?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia keeps EU, Russia in play ahead of key election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89d8b5081e1518e7620e21a72ef6d618527512dec0e9fc87f33356eb0df18a55</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-keeps-eu-russia-in-play-ahead-of-key-election/a-78543495--c7e6906c3b8c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-keeps-eu-russia-in-play-ahead-of-key-election/a-78543495?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Serbia heads toward an uncertain election, President Aleksandar Vucic is balancing ties with Russia and EU ambitions. But growing geopolitical tensions and pressure at home are narrowing his room to maneuver.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's King Harald dies at 89</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6c7f271fdc955cdf09b850818bce2b90b3087d56bd24f919e5a1d377e8e4f6e</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T08:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-dies-at-89/a-78524572--7cc333ca2b96.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-dies-at-89/a-78524572?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">King Harald is succeeded by his son, who has taken the name King Haakon VIII, with Crown Princess Mette-Marit now queen.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Protesters set fire to migrant camp in Ceuta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1a5771926c626ffc099ef5c3c16783266b6c109cefc08b5d8b1598be52bb92f</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T00:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/protesters-set-fire-to-migrant-camp-in-ceuta/a-78538847--b6ca00ede7c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/protesters-set-fire-to-migrant-camp-in-ceuta/a-78538847?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The unrest comes one month after a mass influx of migrants from Morocco to the Spanish exclave in North Africa.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Thieves steal Bronze Age gold in lightning raid on Villena Museum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3103adb67db83b1b00a98bfdc66a6b18510c11739f050138c3137e4679f8adb1</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T19:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-thieves-steal-bronze-age-gold-in-lightning-raid-on-villena-museum/a-78538027--efad0328ac35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-thieves-steal-bronze-age-gold-in-lightning-raid-on-villena-museum/a-78538027?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of the world's greatest Bronze Age gold collections has been swiped, almost in its entirety, from Villena Museum. A highly professional group of thieves were in and out in four minutes flat before the museum opened.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ratko Mladic, the man behind Srebrenica massacre, dies at 84</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:587bf7e90fe0dceb79d875edd1ec9d41084cd287c842bb98ac46c7195bfbade5</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-the-man-behind-srebrenica-massacre-dies-at-84/a-78536491--3ba004d93183.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-the-man-behind-srebrenica-massacre-dies-at-84/a-78536491?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For many, Ratko Mladic represented the horrors of the Bosnian war. He was convicted of genocide for the Srebrenica massacre and other war crimes. On Thursday, he died in detention at The Hague.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ex-Bosnian Serb military leader Ratko Mladic dead at 84</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ce8aab875335266b6e215d2e4a142c3d70709dd12443e1bc1685d94b98741d</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ex-bosnian-serb-military-leader-ratko-mladic-dead-at-84/a-78531323--cd00ff4e2749.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ex-bosnian-serb-military-leader-ratko-mladic-dead-at-84/a-78531323?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The former Bosnian Serb general was convicted of genocide committed during the bloody 1992-95 war in Bosnia and Herzegovina.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>DW users on life in Russia: 'People are mad as hell'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ed25be540a60604c01016029063a68c9d938539d8519858caeedb979262ed9a</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T11:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-users-on-life-in-russia-people-are-mad-as-hell/a-78523454--29af81fdd53c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-users-on-life-in-russia-people-are-mad-as-hell/a-78523454?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Official polling suggests public sentiment in Russia is deteriorating as economic pressure builds. DW asked its users to share their experiences.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>CDU's Volkmann: Ukraine aid is not charity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4de7ba78a9bce66225005b6115fe98ae6db88ebb94c72a929cd756b41c5868e6</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T08:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cdu-s-volkmann-ukraine-aid-is-not-charity/a-78517659--16a3a142867d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cdu-s-volkmann-ukraine-aid-is-not-charity/a-78517659?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former German Chancellor Helmut Kohl's grandson Johannes Volkmann spoke to DW about why Germany must continue to support Ukraine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Grain exports stall as Ukraine steps up attacks on Russia's Black Sea ports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98f54d17eab3c05d40e02c7bb5adaf851cd62aba092fc5482406fceb80d08a7f</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T18:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/grain-exports-stall-as-ukraine-steps-up-attacks-on-russia-s-black-sea-ports/a-78499629--9d365187595e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/grain-exports-stall-as-ukraine-steps-up-attacks-on-russia-s-black-sea-ports/a-78499629?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian drone strikes on Russian infrastructure on the Black Sea are disrupting grain and oil exports from the port of Novorossiysk and other key hubs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Could Russia's growing fuel crisis help end the Ukraine war?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f9c697ebf0668b5762a5d6312dd126126ce7a39ca015865db40d5db266e9c6e</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-23T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-russia-s-growing-fuel-crisis-help-end-the-ukraine-war/a-78472138--13e3feb97e50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-russia-s-growing-fuel-crisis-help-end-the-ukraine-war/a-78472138?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian attacks on oil refineries have deepened Russia's fuel crisis, with shortages reaching Moscow. Could growing public anger put Putin under pressure?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
